From c033df9c5015e83947bf7a1873aeefc5fd69993b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PyScotch <pyscotch@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:58:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 007/240] Bugfix: validate tree-leaf architectures in one place
 for file loaders and library builders [report R. Perry]

The "tleaf" and "ltleaf" target file loaders and the `SCOTCH_archTleaf()`
and `SCOTCH_archLtleaf()` routines each filled the architecture body on
their own, with different checks. The loaders accepted zero or negative
numbers of levels, which led to out-of-bounds reads in
`archTleafMatchInit()`, let the number of terminal domains overflow, and
checked the size of the label permutation against level boundaries and
the uniqueness of its indices in debug mode only, so that an invalid
permutation led to out-of-bounds reads in `archTleafDomDist()` or to
lost terminal domains. The builders performed no check at all, so that
an out-of-range permutation index led to an out-of-bounds write, and
they left the class pointer set with dangling arrays when an allocation
failed.

Move all checks and allocations into the new `archTleafArchBuild()` and
`archLtleafArchBuild()` routines, which the loaders and the builders
both use, as `archCmpltwArchBuild()` is used. Level counts, level sizes,
link costs, the number of terminal domains, and the permutation size,
range and uniqueness are now checked unconditionally; a permutation
index that is already used is detected while building the inverse
permutation. Architecture fields are set only on success, and
`archTleafArchFree()` leaves an empty architecture and accepts one, so
that a failed build can always be followed by `archExit()`. Loaders read
their data into temporary arrays and free nothing of the architecture
body, which `archLoad()` frees through the class hook.

Add a labeled tree-leaf architecture, the permutation of which spans
two levels, to `test_scotch_arch`.

Refs: COR-06, COR-07, API-10, PS-API-4
